miadi-kit
=========

Run as the account whose plugins you want updated:

    miadi-kit update                          update every kit plugin this account has installed
    miadi-kit update --check                  say what would move, change nothing
    miadi-kit update --harness claude,codex   only these harnesses

One line per checkout and per plugin, then a count. A harness not on PATH is
skipped.

| harness | what miadi-kit runs |
|---|---|
| Claude Code | claude plugin marketplace update, then claude plugin update <id> --scope <scope> |
| Codex | codex plugin add <id> when the kit's local marketplace holds a newer version |
| Copilot CLI | copilot plugin update <name>, for a plugin installed from jgwill/miadi-orchestration-kit:<path> |
| Gemini CLI | nothing: an extension added with gemini extensions link reads the checkout |
| Pi | nothing: a package added with pi install <path> reads the checkout |

A kit checkout that a harness reads in place, and the one MIADI_ORCHESTRATION_KIT_ROOT
names, is fast-forwarded to its upstream. One with commits of its own, or not on a
branch with an upstream, is left as it is, and its line says so.

Running sessions keep the version they started with: start a new one to use an
update.

From a kit checkout without the package:

    source <checkout>/scripts/miadi-kit-plugins.sh
